% GANs~\cite{goodfellow2014gan}, generates audio aligned with video content and timing, such as drum sounds for drumming videos. However, RegNet requires separate training for each video category and has slow inference speeds. To address these issues, Iashin and Rahtu~\cite{iashin2021specvqgan} proposed SpecVQGAN, enabling real-time multi-category V2A generation. SpecVQGAN uses a spectrogram-based audio encoding model built on VQGAN~\cite{esser2021vqgan}, creating a perceptually rich spectrogram codebook to handle various audio types. For visual processing, both RegNet and SpecVQGAN use BN-Inception~\cite{bn} as the visual feature extractor, but SpecVQGAN incorporates GPT-2~\cite{radford2019gpt2} for enhanced video understanding. SpecVQGAN also suggests ResNet-50~\cite{he2016resnet} is superior to BN-Inception for visual feature extraction.

