For rhythmic alignment, Su et al.~\cite{su2021rhythmic} proposed RhythmicNet, a three-stage model for symbolic music generation based on motion rhythms. The model sequentially processes motion-to-music generation through Video2Rhythm, Rhythm2Drum, and Drum2Music stages. It extracts motion key points~\cite{cao2020openpose} to predict beat frames, generates corresponding drum patterns, and finally incorporates additional instrument tracks to produce complete music synchronized with the original human movements.
