In the following definition, we recall that Type \textsc{T} can be \simplecycle, \weakcycle, or \strongcycle.\\
\begin{minipage}{\textwidth}
\begin{mdframed}
    \underline{T \AcyclicTemporization}\smallskip\\
\textbf{Input:} (Static) digraph $D$ \smallskip\\
\textbf{Question:} Does there exist a temporization $\lambda : A(D) \to 2^\mathbb{N} \setminus \{\emptyset\}$ such that $\tG = (D, \lambda)$ admits no temporal cycles of Type T? 
\end{mdframed} 
