% This blocking mechanism allows for only a limited amount of explorations per arc, since every exploration of an arc $a$ which doesn't end in a strong-cycle, will backtrack and change a \texttt{false} in the blocking matrix $B[a]$ to \texttt{true}. Since $B[a]$ contains $4^{(\tau+1)^2}$ values, this can only occur a limited amount of times before all future searches are blocked to go through $a$, and the result follows.

