\[
\mathcal{R} \simeq \bigoplus_{j=1}^{d/r} \mathcal{A}[x,\sigma]/(x^r - \zeta^j) \simeq \bigoplus_{j=1}^{d/r} \mathcal{k}^{r\times r}.
\]
Assume $\mu_{\mathcal{R}}$ is the multiplication map on $\mathcal{R}$. Let $\varphi_1:\mathcal{R} \to \mathcal{A}[x,\sigma]^{d}$ be the map defined by $\sum_{j=0}^{d-1} a_j x^j + (x^d - 1) \mapsto \sum_{j=0}^{d-1} a_j x^j$ and let $\varphi_2$ be the restriction to $\mathcal{A}[x,\sigma]^{2d}$ of the quotient map $\mathcal{A}[x,\sigma] \to \mathcal{R}$. Then we have $ \mu_\mathcal{R} = \varphi_2 \circ \mu_d   \circ (\varphi_1 \times \varphi_1)$. By \eqref{eqn:rank restriction} and Theorem~\ref{thm5}, we may conclude that $d r^{\omega-1} \le \rank_{\mathcal{k}} (\mu_d)$.
