Next $\varphi(f)$ is an $r\times r$ matrix of the same form as those in Lemma~\ref{lem15}, thus the multiplication of such matrices costs $\widetilde{O}(d^{\omega-1} r )$ operations. Lastly, given $P = (P_{ij}) \in \mathcal{k}^{r\times r}$, $\psi(P) = \sum_{i=0}^{r-1} (\sum_{j=0}^{r-1} P_{ij} e_i ) x^{j-i \pmod{r}}$ by definition. Thus $\psi(P)$ costs no arithmetic operations and Algorithm~\ref{alg-1} costs $\widetilde{O}( d^{\omega-1} r )$ operations.
