Next we discuss the cost of rewriting $\sum_{i=0}^{d} \sum_{j=0}^{r-1} \lambda_{ij} X^i A^j$ in $\left( \mathcal{k} \langle X, A \rangle/J_1 \right)^{d,r-1}$ in the form $\sum_{i=0}^{d}\sum_{j=0}^{r-1}\mu_{ij} A^{j}X^{i}$. We remark that in the case of Kummer extension discussed in Subsection~\ref{subsec:kummer}, it is easy to see that rewriting $\sum_{i=0}^{d} \sum_{j=0}^{r-1} \lambda_{ij} X^i A^j\in \left( \mathcal{k} \langle X, A \rangle/I_1 \right)^{d,r-1}$  as $\sum_{i=0}^{d}\sum_{j=0}^{r-1}\mu_{ij} A^{j}X^{i}$ costs $\widetilde{O}(dr)$ arithmetic operations, since $\mu_{ij} = \lambda_{ij} \zeta^{ij}$ by $X A = A X$. However, the rewriting procedure becomes more complicated in the case of Artin extension, since $XA = AX + X$ in $\mathcal{k} \langle X, A \rangle/J_1$.   
%A little different from Kummer extension,  we need an algorithm to exchange the position of $y$ and $z$ of an element in $K\langle y,z\rangle/J_{1}(d,r-1)$
\begin{algorithm}[!hbpt]
