for some $g_0,\dots, g_{r_1-1}, h_0,\dots, h_{r_1-1}\in \mathcal{A}_2[x,\sigma^{r_1}]^{\lceil d/r_1 \rceil}$. According to our assumption, one can find $g_j$'s and $h_j$'s by $\widetilde{O}(dr_{1})$ arithmetic operations, since the re-writing can be done by rearranging terms and computing automorphisms.

We notice that $f_1 f_2 =\sum_{k=0}^{r_{1}-1}\sum_{l=0}^{r_{1}-1}x^{k}g_{k}(x^{r_{1}})h_{l}(x^{r_{1}})x^{l}$.
%    Then 
