\subsection{Link Prediction Results}

Table \ref{tab:reddit_title_metrics} presents the link prediction results across different metrics for DyGSSM and other state-of-the-art (SOTA) models. As shown, DyGSSM or Light\_DyGSSM outperformed SOTA models in 17 out of 20 cases. In link prediction under classification settings, DyGSSM outperformed all models in terms of accuracy. DTFormer and WinGNN achieved the second-best performance across all datasets. Regarding AUC, DTFormer performed best on the Bitcoin-Alpha and Bitcoin-OTC datasets. For the remaining datasets, DyGSSM achieved the best performance, while WinGNN was the second-best model. Notably, in the DBLP dataset, DyGSSM significantly improved both accuracy and AUC. 

In the ranking setting, including MRR and Recall@10, DyGSSM outperformed SOTA models on four datasets (UCI, Reddit$\_$title, DBLP, and Bitcoin-Alpha). A key observation is that in datasets with smaller snapshots, such as DBLP and UCI, while DyGSSM improved MRR and Recall@10, the increase was not substantial. However, in datasets with larger snapshots, such as Bitcoin-Alpha and Reddit$\_$title, the improvement was more promising. This suggests that as the dataset gets bigger in term of snapshot, SSM   effectively can captures long-range dependencies in those datasets. Similar trend was seen in Bitcoin-OTC dataset where DyGSSM had a substantial improvement over SOTA models. 

Light\_DyGSSM performed as the best method for six cases and second best method for nine cases. Given its less memory requirements, Light\_DyGSSM could be a powerful choice for large datasets. We encountered an Out-Of-Memory (OOM) issue when sampling 1000 negative edges to compute MRR and Recall@10 for DTFormer and DGMamba. To address this, we reduced the number of negative samples to 50 edges for these calculations. Notably, AUC and accuracy remained unaffected by this change. To ensure a fair comparison, we also re-sampled 50 negative edges and recalculated MRR and Recall@10 for the Bitcoin-Alpha, Bitcoin-OTC, DBLP, and Reddit datasets, as presented in Table \ref{tab:50mrr}. We observed that DyGSSM outperformed DTFormer on Reddit-title and Bitcoin-Alpha. On Bitcoin-OTC, DTFormer achieved better MRR and Recall@10, while DyGSSM performed better in Recall@10 on DBLP, DTFormer achieves better MRR on the same dataset. 
