\section{Welfare optimality}\label{sec:WO}
%We gave comprehensive results on the existence and computation in \cref{sec:JS}. 
We now turn to welfare optimal location profiles, which, by definition, always exist. However, as we show next, finding such location profiles is computationally intractable even for some of the simplest classes of DPGs.

\begin{restatable}{theorem}{welfarehardness}\label{thm:welfarehardness}
    Given a DPG $I$ and value $q\in\mathbb{Q}$, it is NP-complete to decide whether there is a location profile $A$ such that $SW_I(A)\geq q$ even if $I$ is \emph{(i)} a path DPG or \emph{(ii)} an enemies and neutrals DPG.
\end{restatable}
\begin{proof}[Proof Sketch]
