\section{Conclusion}
\vspace{-1pt}
% This paper proposes {\method}, an unsupervised, array-agnostic, generative method to separate speech from multi-microphone mixture recordings. {\method} proposes to use a speech diffusion prior and a novel likelihood approximation to enable posterior sampling, which facilitates separation. The result shows our method outperforms other unsupervised methods and 
% performs on par with supervised methods, especially in ad-hoc microphone array settings.
This paper proposes {\method}, an unsupervised, array-agnostic, and generative method to separate speech from multi-channel mixture recordings. {\method} proposes to use a speech diffusion prior and a novel likelihood approximation to enable posterior sampling. The result shows our method outperforms other unsupervised methods and 
performs on par with supervised methods in SDR. We leave future work to explore \method~for more general array inverse problems.
