\subsection{Sheet under uniaxial deformation}\label{s:Ex_diff}

In the first example, the axial stiffness $\EA$ of a planar sheet is first reconstructed based on uniaxial tension. Then, the density is identified based on longitudinal vibrations using the previously calculated $\EA(\xi)$. Only axial deformations are considered.

