\subsubsection{Axial and bending stiffness reconstruction from statics}\label{s:Ex_curv_stif}

Three independent load cases are analyzed: inflation with uniform internal pressure $p = 2F/L$, horizontal force $P_{\,\mathrm{hor.}} = 2\times10^{-5}F$, and vertical force $P_{\,\mathrm{vert.}} = 2\times10^{-5}F$ (see Fig.~\ref{fig:Ex3_Geo}a). The deformed configurations for these three load cases are shown in Fig.~\ref{fig:Ex3_statDef}a--c. Three load levels for each load case are used (10\%, 50\%, and 100\% of the final load); thus, for all cases $n_\mrlc = 3\times3$. The chosen $\EA(\xi)$ is defined by
\eqb{l}
\EA(\xi)/\EAR = \left\{ \begin{array}{rcl}
	5-19\xi         & \mbox{for} & \xi\in[0,0.25]\,,\\
	0.25+(\xi-0.25) & \mbox{for} & \xi\in(0.25,1]\,, \\
\end{array}\right.
\label{e:Ex3A}\eqe
where $\EAR = 100F$, while $\EI(\xi)$ is specified as
\eqb{l}
\EI(\xi)/\EIR = 2.5\xi^2-5\xi+3 \,,\quad \xi\in[0,1]\,,
\label{e:Ex3C}\eqe
in which $\EIR = 0.001FL^2$. A uniform mesh of 8 linear ME is chosen to identify the unknown stiffness fields, which gives $n_\mrvr = 18$ (Fig.~\ref{fig:Ex3_statDef}d). The unknowns are bounded between $0.1\EAR$ and $10\EAR$, and between $0.1\EIR$ and $10\EIR$, respectively. The initial guess for $\EA$ and $\EI$ is fixed to $1.09\EAR$ and $1.09\EIR$, respectively. 
