On theory, the process goes on forever, but a beautiful argument, independently discovered by Goles and Olivos \cite{goles1981} and Poljak and Sura \cite{poljak1983}, show that
% if $|V| = n < \infty$, either $\Clr_n = \Clr_{n - 1}$ or $\Clr_n = \Clr_{n - 2}$.
