    \caption{Simulated $S_{11}$ response for the slotted patch antenna.}
    \label{fig:Patch_s11_slot}
\end{figure}

\subsection{Case 3: The monopole antenna modeling}
The third case is a slotted monopole antenna from the literature. Its description, topology figure, and parameter list figure are scanned from \cite{liu2022efficient} (Fig. \ref{fig:Monopole description}). The strong D2S tool identifies 7 3D solids (substrate, circular patch, horizontal slot, vertical slot, left ground plane, and right ground plane) with 12 parameters (10 parameters in the figure and 2 thickness parameters in the text) and 2 materials. Moreover, we add a prompt to the Parameter tool to correct a typo in \cite{liu2022efficient} ($S_L = M_L + DP_R + 0.2$). The modeled antenna is shown in Fig. \ref{fig:combined_monopole}.

