    \label{fig:combined_monopole}
\end{figure}

\section{Conclusion}
LEAM, an open-source, prompt-only LLM-enabled antenna modeling technique designed for automated antenna modeling, has been presented. Using three cases with complete description, weak description, and multi-modal description (i.e., image and text scanned for the literature), the effectiveness of LEAM has been shown. Particularly, LEAM realized prompt-only (fine-tuning and retrieval-augmented generation are not needed). The effectiveness comes from the proposed systematic framework and the defined tools. To the best of our knowledge, LEAM is the first LLM-based antenna modeling tool. Future works include enhancing LEAM's compatibility with more LLMs (e.g., DeepSeek, Llama) and EM simulation software (e.g., Ansys HFSS, MATLAB Antenna Toolbox).


