\subsection{Framework Overview}
We start by introducing the outlook for our framework. As demonstrated in Figure \ref{fig:method}, our framework contains two loops. The inner loop is the learner, which optimizes the neural network defined by \eqref{eq:NN-Ly} through minimizing the Lyapunov risk \eqref{eq:loss}. The outer loop is the falsifier, which deploys symbolic regression to retrieve an analytical formulation for the neural network, and then generates counterexamples for further optimization. The outer loop is triggered every \(N_{in}\) updates of the inner loop to avoid redundant regressions. This process, including the \(N_{in}\) updates and the symbolic regression, is referred to as one epoch.
