An agent $p$ always issues blocks that follow the latest advanced round $p$ saw.
This means that rounds can be skipped if the agent has been slow sending while the blocklace has advanced. This is useful 
when an agent that has been offline for some time  catches up with the current blocklace before beginning to send blocks of its own.
