    \item In the sealed bid for intention value phase, each VSP sends proposals $x_{i,t}$ to the NSP in units of VC, reflective of their service profit estimates, and applies for a loan of equal VC amount from the bank. The bank allows loans $\mathcal{K}_{t}$ to VSPs based on the $\mathcal{O}(t)$. $\mathcal{K}_{t}$ can be calculated as
    \begin{align}
     \mathcal{K}_{t} = (\mathcal{K}_{1,t},\cdots,\mathcal{K}_{N,t}) = \mathcal{O}(t) \ast \frac{x_{i,t}}{\sum_{j = 1 }^{N}\bm{x}_{j,t}}.
    \end{align}

