    Where \(\theta_{i}\) represents the estimated parameters of the function \(u_i(\cdot)\), \(\Delta\) represents the amount of additional resources to be allocated to each VSP in instances where the aggregated bids from all VSPs exceed the maximum social welfare. If the aggregated bids do not exceed this threshold, \(\Delta = 0\). The expression \(\mathcal{N}(0, \Delta^2 \bm{I})\) denotes a multivariate Gaussian random variable with a mean of zero and a variance of \(\Delta^2\), utilized to add stochastic elements to each allocation of resources. The function \(\text{norm}(\cdot)\) ensures that the total of the resource allocation vector is kept within the permitted bounds, hence adhering to the established resource constraints.

