\paragraph{Convergence.}
In Figure \ref{fig:2}, we present the relative errors obtained for various degrees of approximation, and a sequence of tensor-product meshes with~$h = h_{\bx} = h_t = 2^{-i}$, $i = 4, \ldots, 8$. We observe quasi-optimal convergence rates of order~$\mathcal{O}(h^p)$ in the $H^1(\QT)$ norm and~$\mathcal{O}(h^{p+1})$ in the~$L^2(\QT)$ norm, which is consistent with the theoretical approximation properties of maximal regularity B-splines of degree~$p$.

